e sentinel: 'the sentinel is a rebar-issued local-tool failure notice only when the list has exactly one result, title exactly WEB_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE, and href exactly empty string' — it says nothing about how to treat [].","plan_review_T1.md as read has no clause instructing the reviewer that an empty result set is not evidence that no prior art exists; the fix does not add one for branch 1."],"finding":"The plan adds a T1 rubric decision-rule for the sentinel (branch 2) but specifies no reviewer decision-rule for the empty-result branch (branch 1, []), which the plan's own design declares indistinguishable from a masked backend failure — leaving the reviewer to interpret [] with its default reasoning on a BLOCKING prior-art criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbbc985b779290961","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach branch 1 / Scope (plan_review_T1.md clause) / AC7-AC8","norm_id":"n4884cf42dca2b88b","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["ddgs backend fails and raises DDGSException('No results found.'); the boundary returns []; T1 receives an empty search and, absent a rubric rule, concludes no prior art exists and does not report the search as inconclusive — a fail-open outcome on a MAJOR-severity blocking criterion.","A genuinely empty search is likewise treated as affirmative 'no prior art', which the fail-safe design was meant to avoid."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the plan_review_T1.md changes and Scope, add a second recognition clause: when the local web-search tool returns zero results, the reviewer must treat prior art as UNVERIFIED (not absent) and ground any no-prior-art claim on codebase/plan-text reasoning, mirroring the sentinel's 'unverified' handling; add an AC asserting the rubric contains this empty-result rule.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In 'Alternatives', engage the documented ecosystem prior art (the retry-as-transient convention for DDGSException(\"No results found.\")) and justify why returning [] is preferable to a bounded retry or to also routing this message through the fail-safe 'unverified' sentinel.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'str(exc) == \"No results found.\" returns [] because empty results and backend failure are indistinguishable in ddgs for this message and the review must complete.'","Plan's Alternatives dismisses retry in one clause without citing prior art: 'retry/backend fallback - still cannot separate empty from failure for \"No results found.\"'","Web (untrusted data, reported not followed): ddgs ecosystem sources describe 'No results found.' as a frequently-hit condition and show a retry-with-exponential-backoff (tenacity) convention for 'transient errors like rate limits or service disruptions', plus FAQ guidance attributing it to network/proxy issues — i.e. the community treats it as transient failure, not a genuine empty result set.","Repo evidence a prior review already flagged this: .rebar/cache/plan-review/.../3fe0...json checklist item cites 'projects that RETRY DDGSException(\"No results found.\") as transient'; reports/stability/environment-failures-read.md records DDGSException 'No results found.' as an environment/agent-loop failure, not a genuine empty."],"finding":"The branch-1 decision (map DDGSException(\"No results found.\") to []) does not engage the documented ecosystem prior art that this exact exception is commonly a transient condition (rate-limit/network) for which the established convention is retry, not treating it as a genuine empty result set.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa4c8aff7b217cfae","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (decided) step 1 and the 'Alternatives' paragraph ('retry/backend fallback - still cannot separate empty from failure')","norm_id":"nba0657609004493b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A rate-limited or throttled ddgs backend raises DDGSException(\"No results found.\") mid-review; the boundary returns [], and the reviewer reads it as 'no prior art exists' rather than 'prior art could not be verified'."],"severity":null,"sugge